    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **282 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that owner creation is rejected with HTTP 400 once 20 owners have already been registered on the current day (by registration date).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRegistrationLimitException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` signalling the daily registration cap was hit.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 after assigning the new owner's registration date (defaulting to today), it now checks `isDailyRegistrationLimitReached(...)` and throws `OwnerRegistrationLimitException` before persisting. The new helper counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's date and rejects once the count reaches the `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 20` constant. The check runs before the duplicate telephone/email checks.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `OwnerRegistrationLimitException` returning `400 Bad Request` (mirroring the existing `DuplicateOwnerException` handler, which returns 409).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`** \u2014 added three tests: 20 owners already registered today \u2192 POST returns 400; 19 today \u2192 the 20th succeeds (201); 20 registered *yesterday* \u2192 today's create still succeeds (proving the limit is per-day).\n\nThe limit is keyed on the registration date, so it naturally resets each day and only counts owners registered on the same date as the incoming one.",
